  "instructions": "Collections & Streams final MCQ. This is the last activity of the Course Review and the course's one graded multiple-choice quiz. You have 60 minutes for 30 questions, about 2 minutes each, with no timer on single questions, and together they cover every topic of the course. The questions are new and harder than the topic practice quizzes. You will trace short code, find a bug from what goes wrong, predict the result of a data transformation, or choose a structure or collector for a stated need. Some questions, more often the later ones, combine two topics. The pass mark is 70%. The coding task of the module check is a separate practical."
